WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:07.103
"The day is finally here!"

2
00:00:07.104 --> 00:00:12.281
Ally looked around the parking lot of the Sandville UFO Museum.

3
00:00:12.282 --> 00:00:15.695
"It's going to be great," Mateo said.

4
00:00:15.696 --> 00:00:18.815
"We've got a proven recipe."

5
00:00:18.816 --> 00:00:23.423
"And fantastic helpers!" Kate said, grinning.

6
00:00:23.424 --> 00:00:27.751
"I really appreciate everyone helping me with the cooking," Barry said.

7
00:00:27.752 --> 00:00:29.830
"Of course!" Ally said.

8
00:00:29.831 --> 00:00:33.307
"And Randy is standing by if you need a break.

9
00:00:33.308 --> 00:00:38.552
It was nice of Ray to let us close the diner for the day."

10
00:00:38.553 --> 00:00:40.482
Barry looked nervous.

11
00:00:40.483 --> 00:00:45.460
"What if no one wants the Beta Burgana? What if it seems boring?"

12
00:00:45.461 --> 00:00:49.163
"Oh, people will want it," Ally said.

13
00:00:49.164 --> 00:00:52.314
"Or so I hope!" she thought.

14
00:00:52.315 --> 00:00:56.419
Dawn came running over to the truck, carrying a large bag.

15
00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:00.272
"I made you all some special aprons for the contest."

16
00:01:00.273 --> 00:01:05.832
"Awesome!" The kids all put on the aprons.

17
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:09.998
"You look just like a professional team," Dawn said.

18
00:01:09.999 --> 00:01:17.502
"Go win the contest!"

19
00:01:17.503 --> 00:01:25.986
Soon there was a long line at Rolling Ray's.

20
00:01:25.987 --> 00:01:30.516
"Our line is longer than Pepe's!" Bethany reported.

21
00:01:30.517 --> 00:01:34.068
"Everything is going really well!" Mateo said.

22
00:01:34.069 --> 00:01:37.926
Ally nodded, but she kept looking around uneasily.

23
00:01:37.927 --> 00:01:42.411
Who was the spy? Would somebody try to sabotage them again?

24
00:01:42.412 --> 00:01:46.549
"Without my powers there's not much I can do," she thought.

25
00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:50.750
"But I can still try to find out who's been spying on us.

26
00:01:50.751 --> 00:01:54.739
An Astralian never gives up."

27
00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.846
Dawn reached the front of the line.

28
00:01:56.847 --> 00:01:59.664
"I'll take two burgers, please.

29
00:01:59.665 --> 00:02:04.420
Flo and I set up a blanket on the grass to wait for the results of the judging to come in.

30
00:02:04.421 --> 00:02:14.052
Good luck, kids. Whatever happens, you're all winners!"

31
00:02:14.053 --> 00:02:18.217
Several hours later the teams gathered around a small stage.

32
00:02:18.218 --> 00:02:20.426
A voice came over the loudspeaker.

33
00:02:20.427 --> 00:02:23.354
"This is the moment we've all been waiting for!

34
00:02:23.355 --> 00:02:27.933
Please welcome the host of our show, Mark Marx!"

35
00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:32.399
People applauded as a man came out from behind the curtain.

36
00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.521
"What a fabulous contest!" Mark Marx said.

37
00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:38.690
"We've had a great time in Sandville.

38
00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:42.025
Such a friendly place. Except . . . "

39
00:02:42.026 --> 00:02:47.414
He laughed. "We wish we'd met at least one alien!"

40
00:02:47.415 --> 00:02:51.405
Everyone laughed—everyone except Ally.

41
00:02:51.406 --> 00:02:58.050
"Now, if you've ever seen our show," Mark Marx continued, "you might think we're just a wholesome cooking show.

42
00:02:58.051 --> 00:03:01.732
But behind the scenes, we like to spice up the competition.

43
00:03:01.733 --> 00:03:05.223
Here are some highlights of our behind-the-scenes activity!"

44
00:03:05.224 --> 00:03:10.239
Ally watched as videos played on the screen on the back wall of the stage.

45
00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.922
One food truck's food went bad.

46
00:03:12.923 --> 00:03:16.573
Another team never got their food delivery.

47
00:03:16.574 --> 00:03:18.375
"Huh," Ally thought.

48
00:03:18.376 --> 00:03:22.561
"Rolling Ray's isn't the only truck that had problems."

49
00:03:22.562 --> 00:03:29.570
But then came a video of Jerry cutting the propane and power lines on Rolling Ray's.

50
00:03:29.571 --> 00:03:34.497
"It was you causing all the trouble!" Ally shouted angrily.

51
00:03:34.498 --> 00:03:38.519
"Jerry! You should be ashamed of yourself!"

52
00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:41.766
"Please calm down!" Mark Marx said.

53
00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:43.716
"And don't blame our producer.

54
00:03:43.717 --> 00:03:45.404
It's all harmless fun.

55
00:03:45.405 --> 00:03:48.299
We like to throw a few wrenches in the works!"

56
00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:52.012
"So that's how you cut the line!" Ally cried.

57
00:03:52.013 --> 00:03:54.077
"With a wrench!"

58
00:03:54.078 --> 00:03:59.525
"Sorry about that, Team Rolling Ray's." Mark Marx laughed.

59
00:03:59.526 --> 00:04:02.060
"But it's an important part of the competition.

60
00:04:02.061 --> 00:04:07.797
You see, our winner is chosen not only for the quality of their food, but also for their persistence.

61
00:04:07.798 --> 00:04:11.269
We were impressed how Rolling Ray's never gave up.

62
00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:18.040
So impressed, in fact . . . You're our winners!"

63
00:04:18.041 --> 00:04:25.319
From behind the curtain, Mark Marx pulled an oversize check for five thousand dollars made out to Rolling Ray's.

64
00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.340
"Come and collect your prize!"

65
00:04:27.341 --> 00:04:32.081
Barry, Mateo, Kate, and Bethany all jumped up on the stage.

66
00:04:32.082 --> 00:04:36.496
But Ally stayed where she was, arms folded across her chest.

67
00:04:36.497 --> 00:04:39.198
"I'm happy we won," she thought.

68
00:04:39.199 --> 00:04:41.321
"But I'm mad the show tricked us.

69
00:04:41.322 --> 00:04:47.988
That would never happen on Astralia!" She watched her friends laughing and grinning.

70
00:04:47.989 --> 00:04:51.936
"I guess I'm not becoming human after all!"

71
00:04:51.937 --> 00:04:57.073
Later, when the Rolling Ray's team was cleaning up, Julius came over to help.

72
00:04:57.074 --> 00:05:02.244
"That was fun." Bethany yawned.

73
00:05:02.245 --> 00:05:06.916
"And I can't believe we each get a thousand dollars!"

74
00:05:06.917 --> 00:05:09.858
"You deserve it," Dawn said.

75
00:05:09.859 --> 00:05:12.891
"You worked very hard for this win."

76
00:05:12.892 --> 00:05:16.155
"Now I can take some cooking classes," Barry said.

77
00:05:16.156 --> 00:05:20.600
"And I can get my comic," Mateo said.

78
00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:23.244
"Now that the contest is over . . ."

79
00:05:23.244 --> 00:05:25.899
Julius stepped closer to Ally.

80
00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:29.331
"Can I take you on a real date?"

81
00:05:29.332 --> 00:05:32.178
"Yes!" Ally said.

82
00:05:32.179 --> 00:05:36.244
"But you have to answer my texts," Julius said.

83
00:05:36.245 --> 00:05:41.318
"Maybe you could use your winnings to, um, get a new phone?"

84
00:05:41.319 --> 00:05:45.257
"That's a fantastic idea!" Ally grinned.

85
00:05:45.258 --> 00:05:47.833
"Julius is right," she thought.

86
00:05:47.834 --> 00:05:58.875
"I need Alpha to work properly—especially so we can figure out how to get my powers back!"

